BT 1 0 0 1 0 122.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13.2 TL (This project develops and evaluates PRESTO-R, a routing policy that combines predicted link-degradation risk with) Tj T* (deep reinforcement learning and an explicit cost for changing routes. A discrete-time network simulator supplies noisy) Tj T* -0.110659 Tw (telemetry for one managed flow and background traffic. A gated recurrent unit \(GRU\) predictor estimates near-future link) Tj T* 0 Tw (risk; a deep Q-network \(DQN\) selects among four candidate paths using path condition and risk features. Across) Tj T* (held-out simulations, PRESTO-R reduced route changes substantially relative to predictive DQN while keeping packet) Tj T* (delivery ratio \(PDR\) close to learned baselines. In NSFNET mixed episodes, it averaged 5.20 switches and 0.9625) Tj T* (PDR, compared with 20.99 switches and 0.9608 PDR for predictive DQN. The predictor onset F1 score was 0.5296,) Tj T* (below the 0.70 project target, and PRESTO-R did not satisfy every predeclared comparison against reactive DQN.) Tj T* (Results support a stability benefit within the tested simulator, while motivating improved prediction and validation on) Tj T* (packet-level or real-network traces.) Tj T* ET
